      "title": "Assistant Professor (Economic Theory) - Department of Economics",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant Professor (Economic Theory) - Department of Economics Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: W. P. Carey School of Business: Department of Economics Location Tempe campus Open Date Sep 25, 2026 Description The Department of Economics in the W. P. Carey School of Business at Arizona State University invites applicants for a faculty position in Economic Theory at the rank of Assistant Professor starting Fall 2027. Essential Functions: The candidate must conduct research at the highest levels that can be published at the top journals in Economics; teach economics courses at the undergraduate and graduate level; serve as a research mentor to doctoral students; and interact effectively with colleagues through department service to support and enhance the intellectual atmosphere of the department. Qualifications Required Qualifications: 1) A PhD in Economics or related field by appointment start date or no later than the end of the fall semester. Those who do not have a PhD by the appointment start date will be hired as an Instructor ABD. 2) A promising and ambitious research agenda in Economic Theory Desired Qualifications: 1) A strong research agenda in Economic Theory, with ideally published or forthcoming papers in premier academic journals 2) Teaching experience 3) Demonstrated knowledge of AI tools through innovative teaching practices, cutting-edge research, and/or through leadership in academic or professional communities. Application Instructions Application deadline is November 1, 2026 . Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool.  Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled.  Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter that addresses t