    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192879": {
      "title": "Associate Dean",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Associate Dean Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Barrett, The Honors College Location Downtown campus Open Date Sep 07, 2026 Description Barrett, The Honors College , is seeking an Associate Dean for Barrett on the ASU Downtown campus. The Associate Dean provides strategic leadership for the Downtown Barrett campus and is responsible for delivering a high-impact, high-value, and innovative honors experience for Downtown Barrett students in coordination with the Dean. The Associate Dean is also a key member of the Barrett leadership team, collaborating with the deans to shape and advance college-level initiatives and priorities as well as enhancing the framework for Barrett in multiple locations. We welcome applications from faculty currently serving at Arizona State University in an Honors Faculty Fellow position with the rank of Associate Teaching Professor or Teaching Professor. This role includes 0.5 FTE in administrative responsibilities , and the selected candidate is expected to maintain a 0.5 FTE faculty workload . Essential Functions: Provide leadership and support for the Barrett staff, faculty, and students at the Downtown campus, including direct supervision of at least one staff position; follow college-wide initiatives, processes, and practices to ensure a consistent high-quality Barrett experience across campuses. Assess honors student enrollment, retention, and success at the campus as well as the impact of the Barrett Downtown experience, and implement changes based on those assessments. Continue to articulate the identity of and priorities for Barrett Downtown, reflecting the specific needs and characteristics of that community while also aligning with the college mission and values. Oversee annual budget in line with strategic priorities of the college and the Barrett Downtown community. Coordinate with ASU and Barrett recruitment and admissions teams to continue to grow the Barrett Downtown community. Collaborate with Downtown colleges, leadership, and faculty to develop and refine course offerings, programs, support, and opportunities for Barrett Downtown students. Collaborate with external partners (businesses, state and local government, other institutions, etc.) to develop and continue professional development opportunities for Barrett Downtown students. Communicate with current and prospective students and their families about the Barrett Downtown experience. Work closely with the deans, faculty chair, and senior staff leaders; actively participate in the Barrett leadership team; and represent the college on committees and at events. Other duties as assigned Working Environment The Associate Dean works in a dynamic higher education environment that includes office, classroom, and campus-wide settings. The position requires regular interaction with faculty, staff, students, and community partners. Duties are performed in both individual and group settings, including meetings, presentations, and campus events. The Associate Dean must spend a minimum of 50% of their assigned work time physically present on the Downtown campus performing administrative, supervisory, and student-facing responsibilities. The role may also require presence at other locations as needed to support institutional initiatives and operations. Work is primarily performed in a standard office environment with extended periods of sitting, computer use, and participation in meetings. The position may require occasional evening and weekend work to support campus events, meetings, and special projects. Travel between campuses or to community sites may be required. Qualifications Required qualifications: Terminal degree in field of specialty and qualifications commensurate with a career-track associate teaching or teaching professor position Outstanding skills in communication and collaboration. Demonstrated commitment to advancing the values of the ASU Charter Must be a current Honors Faculty Fellow within Barrett, The Honors College at Arizona State University Desired qualifications: Higher education leadership experience Understanding of the Downtown campus and/or its academic disciplines Application Instructions To apply for this position, please include: A letter of application indicating relevant academic and professional experience CV A list of three professional references with contact information Emailed applications will not be accepted. The application deadline is Monday, September 28, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. For position-related questions on your application, contact the search committee chair, Dean Tara Williams ( Tara.Williams@asu.edu ). Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180740": {
      "title": "2026-2027 Faculty Associate-Success by Design",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In 2026-2027 Faculty Associate-Success by Design Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: University College: Success by Design Location Tempe, Polytechnic, Downtown Phoenix, West Valley Open Date Feb 01, 2026 Deadline Jan 08, 2027 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Faculty of Success by Design in University College at Arizona State University invites applications to establish a pool for Success by Design Faculty Associates for the 2026-2027 academic year. The successful candidate(s) will teach required courses that support students as they leverage their strengths and build skills needed to persist to graduation. Faculty Associates primarily teach: UNI 120, Problem Solving for Success - Students build a strong creative problem-solving practice and learn ways to tackle common problem-solving roadblocks UNI 220, Mindset Connections - Students learn how beliefs, perceptions, mindsets, and choices influence behavior, and how they can leverage an understanding of procrastination, motivation, and habit to their personal advantage. Through our engaging, active classes, students can choose projects and practices that support their growth goals. As part of the Success by Design team, you will facilitate student-centered classes and support student flourishing across multiple dimensions. Faculty Associates should come to their work with a basic understanding of growth mindset, design thinking, strengths-based approaches, and inquiry-based learning. Success by Design faculty will participate in pre-semester training, follow program policies, hold office hours, engage with mentors, and actively engage in up to three faculty meetings during the semester. Faculty Associate positions are one-semester, non-benefits-eligible, fixed-term appointments with no tenure implications, not to exceed an average of 0.40 FTE per semester. The number of courses is contingent upon unit needs, funding, and sufficient enrollment. Salary is based on qualifications and assigned teaching load. Essential Functions Complete Onboarding & Training: Participate in all required preparation activities before teaching. Teach Assigned Course(s): Deliver course content effectively and engage students in learning. Attend Faculty Office Hours: Be available weekly to support students and engage in course feedback discussions. Manage Canvas Course Shell: Maintain course materials, announcements, and communication within the learning platform. Grade Assignments & Provide Feedback: Evaluate student work promptly and offer individualized, constructive, and actionable feedback. Respond to Student Inquiries: Answer questions and provide guidance in a timely and supportive manner. Support Student Development: Encourage and assist students in their academic, career, and personal growth. Engage in our Community of Practice: Partner with a full-time faculty mentor and attend faculty meetings focused on supporting your development as a facilitator. Follow Department Protocols: Adhere to established procedures for addressing student care and support concerns. Submit Final Grades: Ensure grades are submitted accurately and on time by the designated deadline. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field at the time of appointment Evidence of excellent teaching/student support ability Excellent English written and spoken communication skills Desired Qualifications Terminal Degree in a related field Two years of teaching at a post-secondary institution, four years of experience teaching at a high school (9-12th grade), or four years of experience in student support services at a post-secondary institution or high school, e.g., advisor, student counselor, or student psychologist Demonstrated success in meeting the needs of student populations with varied backgrounds and experiences Experience teaching or working with students who are first-year, first-generation, or in the process of academic recovery Experience applying, utilizing, or teaching design thinking, emotional intelligence, social psychology, sociology, or learning science concepts and/or student success strategies Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a team environment Application Instructions To apply, please submit the following electronically via Interfolio. Only electronic submissions will be reviewed. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications must contain: A letter of application addressing the required and desired qualifications Current curriculum vitae or resume Unofficial graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be requested upon hiring. Information for three professional references (name, position, title, e-mail, phone number) Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool through January 8th of 2027 .  Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled.  A background check and official transcripts are required prior to employment. If you have questions, please contact our office at successbydesign@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181435": {
      "title": "Apply - Interfolio",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In 2026-2027 Instructional Professional-Success by Design Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: University College: Success by Design Location Tempe, Polytechnic, Downtown Phoenix, West Valley Open Date Feb 10, 2026 Deadline Jan 08, 2027 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Faculty of Success by Design in University College at Arizona State University invites applications to establish a pool for Success by Design Instructional Professionals for the 2026-2027 academic year. The successful candidate(s) will teach required courses that support students as they leverage their strengths and build skills needed to persist to graduation. Instructional Professionals primarily teach: UNI 120, Problem Solving for Success - Students build a strong, creative problem-solving practice and learn ways to tackle common problem-solving roadblocks UNI 220, Mindset Connections - Students learn how beliefs, perceptions, mindsets, and choices influence behavior, and how they can leverage an understanding of procrastination, motivation, and habit to their personal advantage. Through our engaging, active classes, students can choose projects and practices that support their growth goals. As part of the Success by Design team, you will facilitate student-centered classes and support student flourishing across multiple dimensions. Instructional Professionals should come to their work with a basic understanding of growth mindset, design thinking, strengths-based approaches, and inquiry-based learning. Success by Design faculty will participate in pre-semester training, follow program policies, hold office hours, engage with mentors, and actively engage in up to three faculty meetings during the semester. Instructional Professional positions are one-semester, non-benefits-eligible, fixed-term appointments with no tenure implications, not to exceed an average of 0.40 FTE per semester. The number of courses is contingent upon unit needs, funding, and sufficient enrollment. Salary is based on qualifications and assigned teaching load. Essential Functions Complete Onboarding & Training: Participate in all required preparation activities before teaching. Teach Assigned Course(s): Deliver course content effectively and engage students in learning. Attend Faculty Office Hours: Be available weekly to support students and engage in course feedback discussions. Manage Canvas Course Shell: Maintain course materials, announcements, and communication within the learning platform. Grade Assignments & Provide Feedback: Evaluate student work promptly and offer individualized, constructive, and actionable feedback. Respond to Student Inquiries: Answer questions and provide guidance in a timely and supportive manner. Support Student Development: Encourage and assist students in their academic, career, and personal growth. Engage in our Community of Practice: Partner with a full-time faculty mentor and attend faculty meetings focused on supporting your development as a facilitator. Follow Department Protocols: Adhere to established procedures for addressing student care and support concerns. Submit Final Grades: Ensure grades are submitted accurately and on time by the designated deadline. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field at the time of appointment Evidence of excellent teaching/student support ability Excellent English written and spoken communication skills Desired Qualifications Terminal Degree in a related field Two years of teaching at a post-secondary institution, four years of experience teaching at a high school (9-12th grade), or four years of experience in student support services at a post-secondary institution or high school, e.g., advisor, student counselor, or student psychologist Demonstrated success in meeting the needs of student populations with varied backgrounds and experiences Experience teaching or working with students who are first-year, first-generation, or in the process of academic recovery Experience applying, utilizing, or teaching design thinking, emotional intelligence, social psychology, sociology, or learning science concepts and/or student success strategies Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a team environment Application Instructions To apply, submit the following electronically via Interfolio. Only electronic submissions will be reviewed. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications must contain: A letter of application addressing the required and desired qualifications Current curriculum vitae or resume Unofficial graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be requested upon hiring. Information for three professional references (name, position, title, e-mail, phone number) Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool through January 8th of 2027. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled.  A background check and official transcripts are required prior to employment. If you have questions, please contact our office at successbydesign@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
